   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1.1: 
a) Coverage and effectiveness of the hydrometric monitoring networks in riparian countries.
b) Number of new observation stations installed
Indicator 1.2: 
Level of introduction of modelling tools and technologies for the strategic flood risk assessment and flood hazard mapping
Indicator 1.3. 
Level of implementation of the systematic gender-responsive socio-economic vulnerability assessment in the DRB
Indicator 2.1: 
State of the Drin River Basin FRM Policy Framework and cooperation on flood risk management 
Indicator 2.2. 
a) % increase in institutional capacity to promote integrated climate resilient flood risk management
b) Number of staff from targeted institutions trained to respond to impacts of climate-related events 
Indicator 2.3. 
State of Drin River Basin Integrated CCA and FRM Strategy
Indicator 3.1: 
State of climate-responsive design of structural and non-structural measures for long-term FRM investment in DRB.  
Indicator 3.2: 
(a) Number of people directly protected from flood risks through structural measures at 3 high risk sites in Albania, Republic of North Macedonia and Montenegro
(b) Area of land protected from flood risks through structural measures at Drin FRM project 3 sites
Indicator 3.3:
(a) number of communities across DRB supported with non-structural measures and adaptation planning (including training, participatory planning and implementation)
(b) scale of agroforestry measures implemented (ha)</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1: 
1.1: Significant gaps in the coverage (especially in Republic of North Macedonia and Montenegro) and inefficiencies in data management, operations and maintenances of the hydrometric monitoring network across DRB prevents adequate forecasting and early warning and efficient decision making on FRM
1.2: a) No integrated basin wide hydrological and hydraulic model for the DRB. Under the new GIZ project detailed flood modeling and mapping is planned for the Shkoder/Skadar Lake and lower Drin and Bojana/Buna area
b) Lack of socio-economic data for risk, damages, losses, exposure and vulnerability assessments
1.3: 0
Outcome 2
2.1 Limited basin-level coordination and cooperation on flood risk management. Under an MoU between the national hydromet institutions there is cooperation and data exchange for flood warning, based on regional forecasts, EFAS and SEE FFG. The Drin Coordinated Action was established to promote joint action for the coordinated integrated management of the shared water resources in the basin. The MoU does not currently specifically address joint actions required for cooperation on flood risk management. 
2.2 Institutional capacities at the regional, national and sub-national level across the basin are insufficient to secure climate-resilient FRM
2.3 The existing coordination and bilateral agreements are insufficient for a truly transboundary river basin approach to flood risk management. What is missing is a basin-level integrated climate change adaptation and flood risk management strategy and plan and a multi-lateral Framework Agreement for the DRB in the field of flood risk management which establishes the institutional and legal basis for cooperation
Outcome 3
Communities of the DRB remain highly exposed to flooding. In the Riparian countries of the DRB, flood defense and flood risk management are done in a reactive manner and as budgets allow. Relevant institutions have limited annual budgets to address urgent issues like structural d</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator target 1.1. 
b) Target number of new stations to be defined during Year1 of the project based on the network design
Indicator target 1.2. 
Enhanced modelling tools and technologies for the strategic flood risk assessment in DRB based on EUFD, including: 
b) Detailed topographic surveys and data for the Crn Drim in Macedonia.
Indicator target 1.2
Gender-responsive socio-economic vulnerability assessments in DRB have been completed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target 1.1:
b) Target number of new stations identified and 25 of the new hydro-meteorological stations, defined in coordination with National Hydromet Service in North Macedonia (UHMR) procured: 3 new fully automated meteorological stations, 5 rain gauge stations, 6 fully automated hydrological stations and 11 piezometering stations.
Target 1.2:
b) ToR for detailed areal surveillance using LiDAR technology of 4,125 sq. kilometers in the Crn Drim River Basin in North Macedonia defined in coordination with the National Geodetic Authority. Procurement of the surveillance is ongoing.
Target 1.3:
No gender-responsive socio-economic vulnerability assessments in DRB have been completed
Target 3.1:
One structural measure for DRB in North Macedonia designed and executed
Target 3.2:
1,000 people directly protected by the intervention completed at improving hydraulic capacity of the Crni Drim River in the urban part of the Municipality of Struga in North Macedonia</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target 1.1:
b) 25 procured hydro-meteorological stations to be installed in designated locations
Target 1.2:
Enhanced modelling tools and technologies for the strategic flood risk assessment in DRB based on EUFD, including: 
a)	Spatial Data Initiative and data management system; 
b)	Detailed topographic surveys and data for the Crn Drim in Macedonia - Procurement of LiDAR Digital Elevation Models (DEM) data completed
c)	Detailed hydrological and hydraulic modelling for the Crn Drim in Macedonia and high resolution flood hazard inundation maps 
d)	Numerical high-level basin-wide hydrological and hydraulic models of the DRB integrating detailed area-based modeling developed under AF, GIZ and national projects.
Indicator target 3.1:
One flood protection structural measure designed (Restoration of the Sateska Rivebed)designed using climate risk information and cost-benefit appraisal methods</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
